1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,253
What if Earth had a ten-second rewind button?

2
00:00:03,293 --> 00:00:05,416
You spill coffee on your laptop,

3
00:00:05,456 --> 00:00:07,918
panic, and slap the big red button on

4
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:08,865
the lamp post.

5
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:10,555
The whole planet rewinds.

6
00:00:10,595 --> 00:00:12,989
The coffee flies back into your cup.

7
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,695
Everyone walks backward for ten seconds.

8
00:00:16,735 --> 00:00:17,649
Pigeons un-poop.

9
00:00:17,689 --> 00:00:19,200
A delivery truck un-honks.

10
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:21,048
Nobody remembers it except you,

11
00:00:21,088 --> 00:00:24,268
standing there holding the button like a magic remote.

12
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,894
You start fixing small things.

13
00:00:26,934 --> 00:00:28,423
A trip on the stairs.

14
00:00:28,463 --> 00:00:29,661
A typo in a text.

15
00:00:29,701 --> 00:00:30,898
An awkward hello.

16
00:00:30,938 --> 00:00:35,121
With ten seconds, you become the smoothest person in town.

17
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,932
Then everyone finds the button.

18
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:39,888
The queue stretches for miles.

19
00:00:39,928 --> 00:00:42,171
Every press undoes somebody else's,

20
00:00:42,211 --> 00:00:44,714
and the same ten seconds loop again and

21
00:00:44,754 --> 00:00:46,671
again, like a skipping record.

22
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:48,398
Arguments get weird.

23
00:00:48,438 --> 00:00:49,879
You say something rude,

24
00:00:49,919 --> 00:00:52,519
slap the button, and the words slide back

25
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:53,549
into your mouth.

26
00:00:53,589 --> 00:00:57,734
Honestly, this should have been invented for every family dinner.

27
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,282
Scientists say a real rewind would need to

28
00:01:01,322 --> 00:01:03,617
reverse entropy itself, which is,

29
00:01:03,657 --> 00:01:05,810
to put it politely, impossible.

30
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:07,792
But as a thought experiment,

31
00:01:07,832 --> 00:01:09,773
it is a lovely idea to hold.

32
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:13,123
Twist: you are the only one who remembers.

33
00:01:13,163 --> 00:01:15,759
So you save the button for one moment:

34
00:01:15,799 --> 00:01:17,840
your niece's very first laugh.

35
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,921
You rewind it again and again,

36
00:01:19,961 --> 00:01:21,794
until the day finally ends.

37
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:24,031
Then you let go.

38
00:01:24,071 --> 00:01:26,903
Time moves forward, soft and unstoppable.

39
00:01:26,943 --> 00:01:29,775
The button sits quietly on the lamp post,

40
00:01:29,815 --> 00:01:33,278
waiting for a moment you would never want to lose.
